Title: Update to random access test cases for IoT NTN test Reason for change: The Information Bit Payload of 72 bits in RMC is too small to accommodate both Contention Resolution Identity MAC control element (9 bytes = 72 bits) and the UE Contention Resolution Identity (48 bits). In NPRACH Resource Level 1, the SIB is repeated, which may lead to collision with the RAR in NPDCCH, potentially result in the RAR being dropped due to the limited size of the RAR window. Summary of change: Corespecalign to TS36.133 ia0 (RAN4 CR R4-2506490). Increase Information Bit Payload to 144bits. Increase parameter ra-ResponseWindowSize and Update parameter npdcch-StartSF-CSS-RA. Consequences if not approved: RAN5 spec will not be aligned with core spec. Clauses affected: 13.3.2.2, 13.3.2.3

